# Docker build context filter — deny-all, then allow.
#
# WHY deny-all instead of a list of exclusions: the build context does NOT read
# .gitignore. `trading-bot/data/` holds trading.db, whose `settings` table
# carries venue api_key/api_secret/password in cleartext (venues.py
# _SECRET_FIELDS), and `trading-bot/state/` holds `dashboard_token` (0600) and
# the news-agent logs. A deny-list leaks the day someone adds a new secret path
# and forgets to come back here. With deny-all, a file that nobody has
# explicitly allowed cannot enter a layer, so the failure mode of forgetting is
# a missing file at build time — loud — instead of a credential in an image
# layer — silent, and permanent once pushed.
#
# An image layer is forever: `docker history` and any registry copy keep it
# even after a later layer deletes the file. Treat every line below as a
# decision about what is safe to publish.

# ---- deny everything at the root -------------------------------------------
*

# ---- allow only what the runtime imports -----------------------------------
!trading-bot

# The container's PID 1, its healthcheck and the dashboard launcher are COPYed
# from here. Only this subdirectory: scripts/windows/ is PowerShell for the
# retired MT5 host and has no business in a Linux image.
!scripts/deploy

# ---- ...minus the parts of trading-bot/ that must never ship ----------------
# Runtime state. data/ = the SQLite DB (credentials, trade history).
# state/ = dashboard_token, logs, decision traces.
trading-bot/data
trading-bot/state
trading-bot/.backups

# trading-bot/tests/ is deliberately KEPT. It is a few KB of pure Python with
# no network and no venue, and shipping it is what lets the runbook prove the
# image itself is sound (`docker compose run --rm engine python
# tests/test_risk_rails.py`) rather than trusting that a green CI run on a
# GitHub runner says anything about this artefact.

# Bytecode compiled against another platform's Python.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]

# Belt and braces: even if one of the directory rules above is ever edited
# away, no database, log, token or dotenv file can ride along.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.corrupt-*
**/*.bad-*
**/*.log
**/.env
**/*.env
**/secrets.*
**/*secret*.yaml
**/*secret*.yml
**/dashboard_token
**/hallucination_check.jsonl

# config.yaml ships (it is startup defaults only, and CLAUDE.md forbids
# secrets in it). config.example.yaml is the committed template — redundant
# inside the image.
trading-bot/config.example.yaml

# The MT5 leg is retired as the primary path (docs/DEPLOYMENT-LINUX.md §1).
# The EA is a Windows/MQL5 artefact that a Linux container can never run;
# 90 KB of it in every layer buys nothing.
**/*.mq5
